ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION of the G2/REVERSAL stream. READ-ONLY: no package
source touched, no version bump, no PR.

Reproduced the committed G2 script end-to-end at rc425 / registry 649 /
numpy-absent. All 157 records re-derive; every reported number matches.

FV1 REFUTED — the stream lead measurement is ENTAILED, not observed.
  The census compares P2 (Y·X == Z) against Q1 (X-1·Y-1 == Z-1) on the left
  reading, and P1 against Q2 on the right. Both pairs collapse under
  (ab)-1 = b-1 a-1 plus bijectivity of inv, and the SAME script measures that
  law TOTAL on all five carriers. Built an order-5 loop with a unique
  two-sided inverse where the law FAILS (13/25): there chiral != forward as
  SETS (|F|=65 |C|=89, F-C=12, C-F=36). So the instrument cannot return
  otherwise on any carrier the stream used.

FV3 REFUTED — chiral_reversal is one shipped chiral_flip call over a mapped
  word, zero decision branches: the shape music/relations.py:57-60 already
  REJECTED three ops for. The spec cites that precedent against
  gustafson_bound() but not against its own op 1.

FV2 BOUNDED — NC3 is VACUOUS on the abelian rows (4 of 8 measured).
  My sub-prediction that NC3 is count-only-decided at O16 was NOT confirmed:
  the SET agrees with the count on every row.

FV4 EMPTY — re-ran the prior-art grep independently against the live 649-op
  registry and the source tree. All four names genuinely ABSENT; the single
  automorph hit is triality_automorphism, adjudicated by reading the def.

Citation spot-check: arXiv:1001.4856 authors/title/affiliations verified
against the abstract page; the abstract confirms the 5/8 bound is NOT stated
there, which is what the stream reported.

